[151.906639, "o", "───────┼─────────┼──────────┼──────────┼──────────────┤\r\n\u001b[C\u001b[m  \u001b[90m│\u001b[m mobile-login \u001b[90m│\u001b[m v4.11.3 \u001b[90m│\u001b[m 425,444  \u001b[90m│\u001b[m 8,334    \u001b[90m│\u001b[m 2.0\u001b[21;66H\u001b[90m│\r\n\u001b[3C├──────────────┼─────────┼──────────┼──────────┼──────────────┤\r\n\u001b[C\u001b[m  \u001b[90m│\u001b[m web-login    \u001b[90m│\u001b[m v7.3.1  \u001b[90m│\u001b[m 710,713  \u001b[90m│\u001b[m 14,330   \u001b[90m│\u001b[m 2.0          \u001b[90m│\u001b[m                                          \r\n   \u001b[90m└──────────────┴─────────┴──────────┴──────────┴──────────────┘\u001b[m                               \r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1K\r\n   The values match, but the optimized run lists \u001b[37m sso-bridge \u001b[m before \u001b[37m mobile-login v4.11.3 \u001b[m. Tho"]
[151.906648, "o", "se rows tie\r\n   at 2.0, so their order isn't guaranteed. This is a tie-order difference, not a data difference.\r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1K\r\n   \u001b[1mEvent count:\u001b[m the event counts are identical (1,421,600). I can't say what each branch of the baseline    \r\n   scanned, so the event count alone doesn't confirm the baseline's \u001b[37m index=* \u001b[m scan matched \u001b[37m demo_soc \u001b[m. The   ┃\r\r\n   matching result rows do support that for this data.                                                      \u001b[B\u001b[1K\r\n   \u001b[1mCaveat:\u001b[m this is one run of each query, so timing could also be affected by caching or load. I'd rerun\r\n   both to confirm.             \u001b[38;3H\u001b[?25h"]
